Leo: Maybe. What would we actually be doing?
Mia: We''d help clean a small lake and plant trees along the bank.
Leo: That sounds tiring. Why does it matter so much?
Mia: The dirty water is driving the birds away. Clean water brings them back.
Leo: I see. So we''re really helping the whole habitat, not just the lake.
Mia: Exactly. And the club will teach us how to record the birds we see.
Leo: All right, count me in. It feels good to do something real.', 'Mia 邀 Leo 周末做自然俱乐部志愿者;任务是清理小湖、在岸边种树;Leo 问为何重要;Mia 说脏水赶走了鸟,清水能让鸟回来;Leo 明白这是在帮整个栖息地;俱乐部还会教他们记录看到的鸟;Leo 答应参加。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"What does the nature club need this weekend?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Volunteers.","More money.","New birds.","A bigger lake."]},{"q":"What will the volunteers do?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["Build a new school.","Clean a lake and plant trees.","Sell trees to the town.","Catch the wild birds."]},{"q":"Why does the work matter, according to Mia?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["The dirty water is driving the birds away.","The lake is too small.","The trees are too old.","The club needs the money."]},{"q":"What will the club teach them?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["How to paint the boats.","How to record the birds they see.","How to swim in the lake.","How to sell the trees."]},{"q":"What does Leo finally decide?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["To stay at home.","To go shopping instead.","To join the activity.","To plant trees alone."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'long', 'elective2', 'U5', 'fltrp');
A hundred years ago, many thousands of tigers lived in the forests of Asia.
Today only a few thousand remain.
People have cut down the forests where tigers hunt, leaving them with less space and less food.
To save the tiger, several countries have set up special reserves where the animals are protected, and in some of these places tiger numbers are slowly rising again.', '野生老虎美丽,却也处境危险;一百年前亚洲森林里有成千上万只老虎;如今只剩几千只;人们砍掉了老虎捕猎的森林,使它们空间和食物变少;为拯救老虎,一些国家设立了保护区,在部分地区老虎数量正缓慢回升。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"What is happening to the wild tiger?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["It is becoming larger.","It is leaving Asia.","It is changing colour.","It is in great danger."]},{"q":"How does the number of tigers today compare with a hundred years ago?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["It is much smaller now.","It is much larger now.","It is exactly the same.","It is unknown."]},{"q":"Why do tigers now have less food and space?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["They eat too much.","Their forests have been cut down.","They moved to the cities.","They stopped hunting."]},{"q":"What have several countries done to help?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["Sold the tigers abroad.","Built more roads.","Set up protected reserves.","Closed all the forests."]},{"q":"What is happening in some of the reserves?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["All the tigers have left.","The forests have disappeared.","Nothing has changed.","Tiger numbers are slowly rising."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'short', 'elective2', 'U5', 'fltrp');
Guide: Not quite. Long ago it was full of seabirds, until people brought rats and cats.
Visitor: And those animals attacked the birds?
Guide: Yes. The number of native birds fell very quickly.
Visitor: So what did people do to put it right?
Guide: They spent years removing the rats and cats, using traps and trained dogs.
Visitor: That must have been hard work.
Guide: It was. But now the seabirds are nesting here again, and the island is finally safe.', '游客问这座岛是否曾几乎没有鸟了;导游说从前满是海鸟,直到有人带来老鼠和猫;那些动物袭击了鸟;本地鸟数量骤降;人们花了数年用陷阱和受训的狗清除老鼠和猫;虽然辛苦,但如今海鸟重新筑巢,岛终于安全了。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"What was the island once full of?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Seabirds.","Tall buildings.","Farm crops.","Visitors."]},{"q":"What caused the bird numbers to fall?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["A long cold winter.","Rats and cats brought by people.","Too many other birds.","A lack of water."]},{"q":"How did people remove the rats and cats?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["By using a strong poison only.","By moving the birds away.","With traps and trained dogs.","By waiting for them to leave."]},{"q":"How long did the work take?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["A single day.","One week.","A few hours.","Many years."]},{"q":"What are the seabirds doing now?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Nesting on the island again.","Leaving the island for good.","Attacking the visitors.","Hiding from the guide."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'long', 'elective2', 'U5', 'fltrp');
On a hot day, the shade under a tree can be several degrees cooler than the open street.
Trees also clean the air by taking in harmful gases and giving out fresh oxygen.
Their roots hold the soil and soak up rainwater, which helps to stop floods.
Birds and insects find food and shelter among the branches, so many cities are now planting more trees along their streets and in their parks.', '树木对城市的作用远不止美观;炎热天树荫比空旷街道凉好几度;树净化空气,吸入有害气体、释放新鲜氧气;树根固土、吸收雨水,有助防洪;鸟和昆虫在枝间觅食栖身,因此许多城市正沿街道和公园多种树。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"What is the main idea of the passage?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["Trees make cities too dark.","Trees do much more than make a city pretty.","Cities should remove their trees.","Trees only matter in forests."]},{"q":"How does a tree help on a hot day?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["It makes the street warmer.","It blocks all the wind.","Its shade keeps the area cooler.","It dries up the rain."]},{"q":"How do trees help the air?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["They add dust to the air.","They make the air hotter.","They stop the wind completely.","They take in harmful gases and give out oxygen."]},{"q":"How do tree roots help stop floods?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["They hold soil and soak up rainwater.","They push the water away.","They block the streets.","They dry out the rivers."]},{"q":"What are many cities doing now?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["Cutting down all trees.","Planting more trees.","Closing their parks.","Building fewer streets."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'short', 'elective2', 'U5', 'fltrp');
Tom: I know. I saw a photo of a turtle caught in a plastic bag.
Anna: We use so much plastic without thinking. Maybe we should cut down.
Tom: Good idea. I could bring my own cloth bag when I go shopping.
Anna: And I''ll carry a metal bottle instead of buying plastic ones.
Tom: Small changes, but if everyone did them, they would really help.
Anna: Let''s also tell our classmates. The more people join, the bigger the difference.
Tom: Agreed. Protecting the sea starts with what we do every day.', 'Anna 读到每年数百万海洋动物因塑料死亡,感到痛心;Tom 见过被塑料袋困住的海龟;两人决定减少用塑料;Tom 购物自带布袋;Anna 用金属瓶代替塑料瓶;小改变若人人都做就有大用;他们还要告诉同学,人越多差别越大;保护海洋从日常做起。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"Why do millions of sea animals die each year?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["Because of the cold.","Because of loud noise.","Because of plastic.","Because of bright light."]},{"q":"What did Tom see in a photo?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["A bird in a tall tree.","A fish in a clean river.","A boat on the sea.","A turtle caught in a plastic bag."]},{"q":"What will Tom do when he goes shopping?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Bring his own cloth bag.","Buy more plastic bags.","Leave his money at home.","Walk instead of drive."]},{"q":"What will Anna use instead of plastic bottles?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["A paper cup.","A metal bottle.","A glass jar.","A wooden box."]},{"q":"What do they decide to ask their classmates to do?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["To buy more bottles.","To stay away from the sea.","To join them in cutting down plastic.","To stop going to school."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'long', 'elective2', 'U5', 'fltrp');
In winter, food can be hard for them to find, so you can hang a small feeder in your garden or on your balcony.
Keep it filled with seeds and clean water, and the birds will soon come to visit.
Try not to make loud noises that might frighten them away.
Planting a few native bushes also gives them a safe place to rest, so with just a little effort you can turn your home into a friendly stop for the birds.', '这里有个帮助家附近野鸟的简单方法;冬天它们难觅食,可在花园或阳台挂个小喂食器;装满种子和干净的水,鸟很快就会来;别发出可能吓走它们的大声;种几丛本地灌木也能给它们安全的歇息处,只需一点努力,家就能成为鸟儿友好的歇脚地。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"Who is this tip mainly for?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["People who sell birds.","People who dislike birds.","People who study fish.","People who want to help wild birds."]},{"q":"Why is winter hard for the birds?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Food is hard to find.","The days are too long.","There are too many feeders.","The water is too warm."]},{"q":"What should you put in the feeder?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["Salt and sand.","Seeds and clean water.","Paper and glue.","Stones and leaves."]},{"q":"What should you avoid doing?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["Filling the feeder too often.","Planting native bushes.","Making loud noises that frighten the birds.","Watching the birds quietly."]},{"q":"How do native bushes help the birds?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["They block out all the light.","They scare the birds away.","They take the place of food.","They give birds a safe place to rest."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'short', 'elective2', 'U5', 'fltrp');

